{{also|Badminton|bádminton|bàdminton|badmínton}}
==English==
[[Image:Badminton Peter Gade.jpg|thumb|right|150px|Badminton player Peter Gade.]]

===Etymology===
Named after [[Badminton]] House, an estate in [[Gloucestershire]] owned by the {{w|Duke of Beaufort}}, where the game was first played in England.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-badminton.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{IPA|/ˈbæd.mɪn.tən/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# A [[racquet]] sport played indoors on a [[court]] by two opposing players (singles) or two opposing pairs of players (doubles), in which a [[shuttlecock]] is [[volley]]ed over a net and the competitions are presided by an [[umpire]] in British English and a [[referee]] in American English.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|badders}} (''UK, informal'')

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|badminton court}}
* {{l|en|badminton player}}

